WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.099 --> 00:00:08.150
Within a roughly 24 hour period, the Joe Biden
presidency took a major, major hit with Joe

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.080
Bob, Joe Biden, not Joe Balmer.

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:18.250
Joe Biden bombing Syria while appearing to
back away from requiring the inclusion of

00:00:18.250 --> 00:00:23.480
a 15 dollar federal minimum wage in the covid
relief bill that's working its way through

00:00:23.480 --> 00:00:26.010
Congress now on the minimum wage.

00:00:26.010 --> 00:00:30.480
The Biden administration has come out and
said, we're still committed to that.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:32.870
We might just do it outside of the covid relief
bill.

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.530
We'll get into that in a moment.

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:39.010
But not a good 24 hours for Joe Biden here.

00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:42.800
On Thursday, Joe Biden launched airstrikes
in Syria.

00:00:42.800 --> 00:00:44.489
Now, why did Joe Biden do this?

00:00:44.489 --> 00:00:46.729
Well, he explained it or at least tried to.

00:00:46.729 --> 00:00:51.819
In a letter to congressional leadership, Joe
Biden said the strike was, quote, pursuant

00:00:51.819 --> 00:00:58.489
to the United States inherent right of self-defense,
as reflected in Article 51 of the United Nations

00:00:58.489 --> 00:00:59.489
charter.

00:00:59.489 --> 00:01:02.069
Biden further explaining that quote, At my
direction.

00:01:02.069 --> 00:01:08.020
On February 25th, U.S. forces conducted a
targeted military strike against infrastructure

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:13.549
in eastern Syria used by Iran, supported non-state
militia groups.

00:01:13.549 --> 00:01:17.710
Those non-state militia groups were involved
in recent attacks against United States and

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:25.090
coalition personnel in Iraq, including the
February 15 attack in Irbil, Iraq, which wounded

00:01:25.090 --> 00:01:30.420
one U.S. service member, wounded four U.S.
contractors, including one critically, and

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:33.840
killed one Filipino contractor.

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:35.640
However.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:42.590
We are right back to the same issue of a president
obtaining authorization for use of military

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:47.119
force through Congress, this was an issue
with Barack Obama.

00:01:47.119 --> 00:01:49.119
This was an issue with Donald Trump.

00:01:49.119 --> 00:01:50.890
This is now an issue with Joe Biden.

00:01:50.890 --> 00:01:53.039
So there are two things here.

00:01:53.039 --> 00:01:56.289
First are the particulars of these strikes.

00:01:56.289 --> 00:02:03.950
This is just the latest of 20 years of American
foreign policy all over again since 9/11.

00:02:03.950 --> 00:02:06.950
They attacked U.S. personnel in Iraq.

00:02:06.950 --> 00:02:08.170
So we're retaliating.

00:02:08.170 --> 00:02:10.450
OK, well, so what's the point here?

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:14.480
The point is to send the message that we won't
tolerate this.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:15.540
All right.

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:17.220
And then what happens next?

00:02:17.220 --> 00:02:22.590
The attack sours any goodwill that there was
to the United States.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:23.680
Nothing improves.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:27.130
We rinse and repeat for another five years
of the same stuff.

00:02:27.130 --> 00:02:33.660
So I don't really care to debate whether this
particular case well, there was a service

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:37.500
member wounded and four contractors and a
Filipino killed.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:42.140
And so this was justified because of that
attack, to be honest.

00:02:42.140 --> 00:02:50.290
Maybe it was under this completely sort of
deranged framework in which we've been operating

00:02:50.290 --> 00:02:51.540
for the last 20 years.

00:02:51.540 --> 00:02:54.080
Maybe it was justified in that framework.

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.190
Maybe it wasn't.

00:02:55.190 --> 00:03:02.850
The questions are to, number one, will we
ever have a president who actually dislodges

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:09.300
the decades long status quo of repeating things
that don't work and just extend the status

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:10.450
quo?

00:03:10.450 --> 00:03:15.140
This obviously isn't going to do that, regardless
of your opinion about this particular strike.

00:03:15.140 --> 00:03:19.420
And then further, we once again get to this
issue of an authorization to use military

00:03:19.420 --> 00:03:20.420
force.

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:28.660
This all goes back to resolutions from 2001
and 2002, which were passed to give the president

00:03:28.660 --> 00:03:34.050
the ability to go after the then president,
George W. Bush, to go after those who did

00:03:34.050 --> 00:03:36.050
the September 11th attacks.

00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:42.650
It was used to go into war with Iraq in 2003,
which didn't do the September 11th attacks.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:50.390
But then it has been subsequently used to
as the legal justification for a whole bunch

00:03:50.390 --> 00:03:54.920
of these different strikes, U.S. strikes in
Syria, U.S. strikes elsewhere.

00:03:54.920 --> 00:04:01.250
And presidents always point back to the 2001
a yump authorization for the use of military

00:04:01.250 --> 00:04:03.530
force as to why they can do it.

00:04:03.530 --> 00:04:05.070
But can they?

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:08.230
Many Democrats say no when it's a Democrat
in office.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:13.310
Many Republicans also say no, although they
tend to shut their mouths when it's a Republican

00:04:13.310 --> 00:04:15.780
in the Oval Office doing the same thing.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.680
So we can't be hypocrites here.

00:04:17.680 --> 00:04:23.730
If the umph didn't cover Trump stuff in Syria,
didn't cover Obama, didn't cover things George

00:04:23.730 --> 00:04:29.020
W. Bush did outside of the scope of responding
to 9/11, it can't cover things that Joe Biden

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.020
does either.

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:31.640
So we just have to pick one.

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:37.420
And I believe at this point, 20 years later,
the argument is definitely no good.

00:04:37.420 --> 00:04:41.340
So for me, this is beyond any debate about
this particular incident, this particular

00:04:41.340 --> 00:04:42.340
bombing.

00:04:42.340 --> 00:04:45.730
This is about more of the same once again,
in these never ending conflicts.

00:04:45.730 --> 00:04:51.730
And then coinciding with the minimum wage
disaster, Joe Biden included a fifteen dollar

00:04:51.730 --> 00:04:53.490
co, rather.

00:04:53.490 --> 00:04:56.580
Coinciding with the serious stuff is the minimum
wage disaster.

00:04:56.580 --> 00:05:02.240
Joe Biden included a 15 dollar minimum wage
in his covid relief bill on technical grounds.

00:05:02.240 --> 00:05:05.450
It's not going to be in the Senate version
of the covid relief bill.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.450
Why?

00:05:06.450 --> 00:05:11.920
The Senate parliamentarian Elizabeth McDonough
says a 15 dollar minimum wage provision doesn't

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.880
comply with rules governing what can be done
via budget reconciliation.

00:05:16.880 --> 00:05:24.000
So almost certainly, even though Kamala Harris
could overrule that decision by the parliamentarian,

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:28.680
the Senate will likely pass a version of covid
relief, not including a 15 dollar minimum

00:05:28.680 --> 00:05:29.680
wage.

00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:31.140
It'll go back to the house.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:35.830
The House will have to vote on that and it
will pass without the fifteen dollar minimum

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:36.860
wage.

00:05:36.860 --> 00:05:44.300
I don't believe that it's clear that a standalone
bill on a 15 dollar minimum wage makes it

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:46.050
actually happen.

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:50.820
That's increasingly what the Biden administration
is pointing to, saying it's too big a step

00:05:50.820 --> 00:05:53.560
to override the Senate parliamentarian.

00:05:53.560 --> 00:05:57.850
We are committed to the 15 dollar minimum
wage, but we will do it separately.

00:05:57.850 --> 00:05:59.050
I don't know if that will happen.

00:05:59.050 --> 00:06:04.300
It's not clear to me that every Democratic
senator wants a 15 dollar minimum wage.

00:06:04.300 --> 00:06:08.790
So overall, not a good 48 hour period for
Joe Biden.

00:06:08.790 --> 00:06:11.139
And we will, of course, be following this
this week

